Fix dispatch offer selection after completed deliveries

Root cause: getDeclinedRequestIdsForDriver() excluded any request the
 driver had ever declined (within the last 300), with no time window.
 A driver who had declined available requests in the past would see "No
deliveries available" after completing a delivery even though those
requests were still valid.

Changes:
- getDeclinedRequestIdsForDriver() now excludes only declines within the
  last 24 hours, matching the intended "recent dispatch window" semantics.
- Extracted pure selection logic into dispatchSelection.ts so the rules
  are unit-testable without a database.
- isOfferableToDriver() now accepts a `now` reference instead of calling
  new Date(), making tests deterministic and behavior consistent.
- Added dispatch.test.ts covering sequential deliveries, priority/age
  ordering, preferred-driver holds, declined-request exclusion, and stale
  pending-offer cleanup.

No cleanup of existing driverOffers records is required; stale pending
offers for already-completed requests are expired automatically on the
next driver portal load.

